<title>FRANCE: Jospin, Kohl agree up to each to meet EMU goals.</title>
<headline>Jospin, Kohl agree up to each to meet EMU goals.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Lionel Jospin said on Friday he had spoken to German Chancellor Helmut Kohl on Thursday and that both agreed it was up to each individual country to work to meet Maastricht treaty criteria.</p>
<p>He had been asked whether Germany supported France's decision to curb its budget deficit this year without aiming to cut it to precisely 3.0 percent of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>He said both he and Kohl believed it was up to individual countries to act on their own to meet Maastricht treaty criteria. Every country must do &quot;freely what it needs to do to reach the common goals,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said he spoke to Kohl on Thursday by telephone.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
</text>
